  of the other outside things that have  made me feel strange you know  um i've never had a problem with  the general fact of of making music or  playing music i've never stopped loving  it  it's been the outside stuff um you know  that has made me feel down at times but  i think there are two things that have  protected me over the course of  my career and the first thing is  enthusiasm  and the second thing is how much i love  music  enthusiasm as soon as you  fail enthusiasm tells you that  the next great idea is around the corner  and  your love of music will always center  your you if you're doing  this for that and that alone because  that is hard to take away you know  people can reduce and criticize other  elements but the fact that  it sounds really really simple but  loving the actual  the actual making of music and the  playing of music is is what i think has  really  helped me balance things thanks for the  question
 

